# Conventional Commits

When creating git commits, follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Type + optional scope + colon + space, then a short description
- Description: imperative mood, concise, no trailing period
- Body (optional): blank line after description; explain *why*, not only *what*
- Footers (optional): blank line after body; `Token: value` or `Token #value`

## Types (use these)

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability (SemVer MINOR) |
| `fix` | Bug fix (SemVer PATCH) |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting; no code meaning change |
| `refactor` | Restructure without feat/fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `build` | Build system or dependencies |
| `ci` | CI config |
| `chore` | Maintenance that doesn’t fit above |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit |

## Scope (optional, preferred when clear)

Use a short noun in parentheses matching the area touched, e.g.:

- `recruitment`, `hero`, `nav`, `footer`, `seo`, `vercel`

Examples from this repo: `feat(recruitment): …`, `fix(hero): …`, `fix(nav): …`

## Breaking changes

- Add `!` after type/scope: `feat(api)!: …`, **or**
- Footer: `BREAKING CHANGE: <description>` (token must be uppercase)

## Good / bad

```
# ✅ GOOD
feat(recruitment): add dedicated apply page with Lottie success
fix(nav): make landing anchor navigation reliable
docs: correct spelling of CHANGELOG

# ❌ BAD
Update stuff
Fixed bug.
feat: Added new form.    # past tense + trailing period
FEAT(Recruitment): Add page  # prefer lowercase type; keep description imperative
```

## Agent checklist

- Only commit when the user asks
- Match this format for every commit message (including HEREDOC commits)
- Prefer one logical change per commit; split mixed types when practical
- Do not invent types outside the table above unless the user requests it
